## PR Title
Install Amazon CloudWatch Agent on Jenkins Controller EC2 Instance

## Description
Updated the Jenkins controller EC2 user-data script (`user_data.tpl`) to automatically download and install the Amazon CloudWatch Agent from the designated S3 bucket during instance initialization.

### Changes Made
- Added CloudWatch Agent RPM download from `s3://jenkins-binaries-213141505949/amazon-cloudwatch-agent.rpm`.
- Added installation using the `dnf` package manager on Amazon Linux 2023.
- Enabled the CloudWatch Agent service to start automatically at boot.
- Added package installation verification.
- Preserved all existing Jenkins controller configurations and startup processes.

### Testing and Validation
- Verify the CloudWatch Agent RPM downloads successfully from S3.
- Confirm the agent installs successfully using `rpm -q amazon-cloudwatch-agent`.
- Verify the service is enabled using `systemctl is-enabled amazon-cloudwatch-agent`.
- Confirm existing Jenkins controller functionality remains unaffected.

### Impact
This change prepares the Jenkins controller EC2 instance for CloudWatch monitoring without modifying existing Jenkins functionality. Additional agent configuration is required to enable metrics and log collection.
